---
// 01 · 질문: 하나의 큰 질문 → 두 질문(상태 · 정보) → 하나의 고리로 모임.
// 제어와 기억은 따로가 아니라 같은 문제예요: 개인의 뇌를 충분히 정확하게 모델링하기.
const loop = ['Observe', 'Infer latent state', 'Predict transition', 'Select perturbation', 'Observe response', 'Update model'];
---
<section class="question" id="question" aria-labelledby="question-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker mono">01 / The question</p>
    <h2 id="question-h">Can we build a model that learns an individual brain?</h2>
    <p class="dek">Precise enough to infer what state it is in and what information it holds, predict how that changes, and know what intervention does to it. Because the same stimulation can produce different responses in different people.</p>

    <div class="two" aria-label="Two questions that converge">
      <div class="q">
        <p class="q-k mono">Control</p>
        <p class="q-t">What state is this brain in?</p>
        <p class="q-c mono">state → prediction → intervention</p>
      </div>
      <div class="q">
        <p class="q-k mono">Memory</p>
        <p class="q-t">What information does it contain?</p>
        <p class="q-c mono">representation → retrieval → accessibility</p>
      </div>
      <svg class="join" viewBox="0 0 1000 70" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M250 0 C250 40 500 30 500 70 M750 0 C750 40 500 30 500 70" />
      </svg>
    </div>

    <ol class="loop mono" aria-label="Shared loop">
      {loop.map((s, i) => <li style={`--i:${i}`}>{s}</li>)}
    </ol>
    <p class="note">Restoring memory may be a harder form of closed-loop control: steering states that carry information, not only symptoms.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .question { --acc: #a8c8ff; background: #000; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-block: clamp(96px, 16vw, 200px) clamp(80px, 12vw, 150px); }
  .kicker { color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0 0 28px; }
  h2 {
    margin: 0; max-width: 17ch; color: #fff;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 6.6vw, 96px); font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .dek { max-width: 54ch; margin: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px) 0 0; color: #a9a9a9; font-size: clamp(17px, 1.5vw, 20px); line-height: 1.6; }

  .two { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0; margin-top: clamp(48px, 7vw, 80px); border-top: 1px solid #262626; border-left: 1px solid #262626; }
  .q { padding: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 28px); border-right: 1px solid #262626; border-bottom: 1px solid #262626; }
  .q-k { margin: 0; color: var(--acc); letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .q-t { margin: 10px 0 0; color: #fff; font-size: clamp(22px, 2.4vw, 32px); font-weight: 350; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.2; }
  .q-c { margin: 12px 0 0; color: #8a8a8a; }
  .join { grid-column: 1 / -1; display: block; width: 100%; height: 56px; }
  .join path { fill: none; stroke: #3a3a3a; stroke-width: 1.2; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; }

  .loop {
    list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 16px 18px; border: 1px solid #2c3a4c; background: #04070b;
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 10px 0; color: #8d8d8d; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .loop li { display: flex; align-items: center; animation: q-step 7.2s infinite; animation-delay: calc(var(--i) * 1.2s); }
  .loop li:not(:last-child)::after { content: '→'; color: #4a4a4a; margin: 0 12px; }
  @keyframes q-step { 0%, 12% { color: #a8c8ff; } 18%, 100% { color: #8d8d8d; } }
  .note { max-width: 60ch; margin: 18px auto 0; text-align: center; color: #9a9a9a; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.6; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .two { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .join { display: none; }
    .loop { margin-top: 0; justify-content: flex-start; }
    .note { text-align: left; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .loop li { animation: none; } }
</style>
